// Gobannos (placeholder), a smith of the craftsmen's quarter at Bibracte.
// Sells arms. Half his iron is spoken for.
=== start
The smithy is a roofed yard full of heat and noise, and a man with forearms like hams is drawing out a spearhead on the anvil. He finishes the heat before he looks up.

"Gobannos," he says, in a voice ruined by smoke. "Buying or looking?"
* "Show me what you have." -> trade
* "Who's all this iron for?" -> iron
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== trade
~ barter

=== iron
He looks at the racks of spearheads, a hundred of them at least, black and new. "Somebody who pays on time," he says. "Half of it's spoken for, and I don't say by whom."
[flag dan_met] He glances up the hill, though, when he says it.
* "Show me what you have." -> trade
* "Goodbye." -> END
